From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 03:09:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] DVDDemuxFFmpeg: a Blu-ray stream set up again is not its own
 duplicate

A Blu-ray carries some streams twice under one PID, a TrueHD stream and
its AC-3 core for one, and AddStream discards a stream whose PID and
type it already has. When a stream is set up again, on a change of
picture size or of audio channels, the stream it replaces is still in
the map under the same index, so the new one was taken for a duplicate
of it and discarded: ffmpeg stopped returning its packets, and the
stream was lost until the demuxer next created its streams.

The stream under the index being set up is no longer compared.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
index df1768f..d523125 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -2690,9 +2690,11 @@ CDemuxStream* CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::AddStream(int streamIdx)
       }
       stream->dvdNavId = pStream->id;
 
+      // the stream this one replaces is no duplicate
       auto it = std::find_if(m_streams.begin(), m_streams.end(),
-        [&stream](const std::pair<int, CDemuxStream*>& v)
-        {return (v.second->dvdNavId == stream->dvdNavId) && (v.second->type == stream->type); });
+        [&stream, streamIdx](const std::pair<int, CDemuxStream*>& v)
+        {return v.first != streamIdx && (v.second->dvdNavId == stream->dvdNavId) &&
+                (v.second->type == stream->type); });
 
       if (it != m_streams.end())
       {
